<title>SPAIN: EU agreed to raise Spain 95 deficit/gdp to 6.6%.</title>
<headline>EU agreed to raise Spain 95 deficit/gdp to 6.6%.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission agreed to ascribe the 721 billion pesetas surprise hole discovered in July this year to Spain's 1995 budget, Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato told parliament on Tuesday according to local reports.</p>
<p>That means that the Spanish 1995 deficit rose to 6.6 percent of gross domestic product from the previous 5.8 percent. That won't put in any danger the payment to Spain from the European Cohesion Fund which is linked to the convergence process, Rato said.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2159</p>
